If you don't have a way of checking your pet's HP, don't let it take on
too many guards in a row.  At level 9 your pet is about the same
strength as a guard.  It can kill them, but they can also kill it.  And
if you're level 1 in Minetown with no pet you are in  t r o u b l e.
Assuming you have a cat or dog of course.  Though the only other decent
pet I can envision a racketeer having is a djinn.

You can get a fair amount of cash just by selling everything you find
up until Minetown and looting shops, so you can probably get a pretty
low AC buying protection at level 2.  Level 2 is a lot easier than
level 1 - you get almost double the HP and enough MP to cast more than
1 spell in a row (my racketeers are usually healers, and my level 2
healers fare a lot better than the level 1's, and also end up with more
protection because the level 1 healers DIE).


